.TH BOOTSTRAP.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-cluster-tools 1.0.1" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- create the mu2edaq-cluster-tools development venv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.RB [ \-\-dev ]
.br
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.BR \-\-version | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates
.I venv/
in the checkout with
.B $PYTHON
(default
.BR python3 ,
3.9 or newer) if it does not exist, activates it, upgrades pip, and installs
the package with its
.I dev
extra (pytest) so that
.B ssh\-selector
and
.B lan\-scan
are on the venv's
.BR PATH .
.PP
The package spec is
.B .[dev]
relative to the
.I current
directory, not the script's, so run the script from the checkout.
For a per-user install with launchers on
.BR PATH ,
use
.BR install.sh (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Install in editable mode
.RB ( "pip install \-e" ).
Without it the install is a regular copy.
The
.I dev
extra is installed either way.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.B mu2edaq\-cluster\-tools
.I version
(read from
.IR src/mu2edaq_cluster_tools/_version.py )
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the script's header comment and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I venv/
The virtual environment, POSIX layout
.RI ( venv/bin/activate ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHON
Interpreter used to create the venv.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No usable Python 3.9+, or a failing venv or pip step
.RB ( "set \-e" ).
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
cd mu2edaq\-cluster\-tools
\&./bootstrap.sh \-\-dev
source venv/bin/activate
pytest
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install.sh (1),
.BR ssh\-selector (1),
.BR lan\-scan (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
